## PART 4: SCORING ENGINE — DEEP TECHNICAL DETAIL

### 4.1 Normalization Pipeline

```
Raw Result
    │
    ▼
BenchmarkingEngine.normalize_score(raw, test_type, age, category)
    │
    ├── Look up settings.TEST_REGISTRY[test_type]["direction"]
    │   ("higher", "lower", or "optimal_band")
    │
    ├── BenchmarkingEngine.resolve_norms(test_type, age, category)
    │   ├── Map category → "Male" / "Female" / "General"
    │   ├── Find bracketing age-band midpoints (8.5, 11, 14, 17, 22)
    │   └── LINEAR INTERPOLATION of mean & std between midpoints
    │       (so a 10-year-old and a 12-year-old score differently)
    │
    ├── Compute z-score or band score:
    │   ├── "higher": z = (raw − mean) / std
    │   ├── "lower":  z = (mean − raw) / std  (smaller time = better)
    │   └── "optimal_band" (BMI):
    │       d = abs(raw − band_center) / half_band_width
    │       if inside band: score = 95 − d × 25   (95 at centre, 70 at edge)
    │       if outside band: score = 70 − z × 24  (drops ~24 pts per std)
    │
    ├── Convert z to percentile: scipy.stats.norm.cdf(z) × 100
    │
    └── Clamp to [1, 99] (floor 1 so geometric mean stays finite)
    │
    ▼
Normalized score (1–99) + Tier label + Benchmark source string
```

### 4.2 Performance Tier Labels

| Score Range | Label |
|---|---|
| ≥ 90 | Elite |
| ≥ 75 | Excellent |
| ≥ 60 | Above Average |
| ≥ 40 | Average |
| ≥ 20 | Developing |
| < 20 | Needs Improvement |

### 4.3 Athletic Performance Index (API)

**Domain → Test mapping:**
```python
DOMAIN_TESTS = {
    "speed":       ["sprint_50m"],
    "agility":     ["shuttle_run"],
    "strength":    ["sit_up"],
    "power":       ["vertical_jump", "broad_jump"],   # averaged
    "endurance":   ["endurance_run"],
    "flexibility": ["sit_and_reach"],   # extra indicator only
}
```

**Formula:**
```
overall_index = exp( Σ[w_d × log(score_d)] / Σ[w_d] )
```
where the sum is over **only the domains that have data** (no domain is counted as zero for a test not yet taken). Weights are equal (0.20 each for the 5 athletic domains) and are **renormalized** for partial batteries.

**Why geometric mean?** It penalizes a single very weak domain more than an arithmetic mean. A 90/90/90/90/10 athlete gets a lower API than 70/70/70/70/70, which is correct — well-rounded athletes beat one-trick performers.

**Untested domains** show a display placeholder of `50.0` (neutral) but **never** contribute to the overall index computation.

